[UnusedOrLegacy]

; --- Commented-out tools in PBB_NativeTools.pb ---
UpdateFunctionsTitle = Update native functions
UpdateFunctionsEx    = To color code elements, PBBrowser lists the native functions of PureBasic by scanning the %quote%PureBasic.chm%quote% help file provided with each version of PureBasic.%newline%By clicking %quote%Execute%quote%, you update this list from the most recent version of PureBasic installed on your computer. By default, this version was used to establish the current list. However, if you have just installed a newer version of PureBasic, it might be helpful to update it. In this case, click 'Execute'.
UpdatePBExeEx        = When you click on a file or procedure name, PBBrowser attempts to open it by sending a message to the PureBasic editor.%newline%If you have multiple versions of PureBasic installed, you may prefer to use one in particular. However, note that if PBBrowser was launched from an editor using the 'Tools' menu or a keyboard shortcut, it will always use that version of the editor until it is called by another version. Thus, if you are working with several versions of PureBasic at the same time, PBBrowser will always respond to the version that initiated a dialogue with it. You can still click 'Execute' to set your preference.

